{"parentUuid":"135eff15-3711-45e9-8a24-f72739cffc57","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae3c21075cb388b14","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WECr9BcZJBov8CHyaKG42n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DN27z4LFzU1wBo8RKGsZuq","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Benders cut sharing parallel decomposition cross-scenario reuse"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4300,"cache_read_input_tokens":21118,"output_tokens":226,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4300},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":21118,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4300,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoreLv139pftj25Xr2br","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"30c94437-d0ec-47af-a439-1e03ba4ed736","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:31.308Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e7765408-bf57-4fad-8942-7b3c66b935e6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"ae3c21075cb388b14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015L1a5Dou5YXMiCuWfpkY95","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT model clone hint warm start performance \"or-tools\"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"✨ Recipes for Google OR-Tools | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/model.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/model.md\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding CP-SAT model cloning, hints, warm start, and performance in OR-Tools:\n\n## Solution Hints and Warm Starting\n\nA solution hint is not a hard constraint; the solver will try to use it in search for a while, and then gradually revert to its default search technique. Some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve the solver's performance if they are good. If the hints actually represent a feasible solution, the solver can use them to prune the search space of all branches that have worse bounds than the hints.\n\n## Hint Requirements and Limitations\n\nWhen reading about hints, the first thing you think is \"this is a way to do warm-starts.\" But hints must cover all variables they touch and remain feasible after presolve or they're ignored. Solution hints don't need to use all variables: partial solution hints are fine.\n\n## Model Cloning\n\nYou can clone a model by using `text_format.Parse(str(model), new_model.Proto())`, which allows you to convert a model to its protobuf representation and parse it into a new model instance.\n\n## Recent Improvements\n\nThe last release 9.12 in February added Python 3.13 support, revamped hint handling, and sped up the linear expression layer.\n\n## Hint Repair and Conflict Management\n\nBecause repairing an infeasible hint can be computationally expensive, CP-SAT handles this process carefully. You can instruct CP-SAT to attempt repairing the hint by setting solver.parameters.repair_hint = True. Additionally, you can adjust the limit on how much effort CP-SAT should spend repairing the hint using solver.parameters.hint_conflict_limit. For example, setting solver.parameters.hint_conflict_limit = 10 controls how many conflicts CP-SAT will resolve before giving up.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b1d1417c-3682-441f-8fff-ba4e7c347e68","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:37.460Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7765408-bf57-4fad-8942-7b3c66b935e6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"135eff15-3711-45e9-8a24-f72739cffc57","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"ae3c21075cb388b14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EfBm3oaiKxkTnxHME53Rhh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"nogood learning constraint programming canonical normalization graph isomorphism nauty\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving the Graph Isomorphism Problem: A Deep Dive into Algorithmic Techniques | Learn Here - WithMe\",\"url\":\"https://www.codingpancake.com/2026/04/solving-graph-isomorphism-problem-deep.html\"},{\"title\":\"nauty and Traces User’s Guide (Version 2.6) Brendan D. McKay∗\",\"url\":\"https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/nauty/nug26.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Graph Isomorphism - Nauty Traces\",\"url\":\"https://pallini.di.uniroma1.it/Introduction.html\"},{\"title\":\"nauty User’s Guide (Version 2.4) Brendan D. McKay∗\",\"url\":\"https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/nauty/nug.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practical graph isomorphism, II - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0747717113001193\"},{\"title\":\"Breaking Symmetries in Graphs: The Nauty Way\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp2016d.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - noamteyssier/graph-canon: Generate canonical labels for graphs built on NAUTY\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/noamteyssier/graph-canon\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Graph Isomorphism II | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/234066554_Practical_Graph_Isomorphism_II\"},{\"title\":\"Practical graph isomorphism, II Brendan D. McKay\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1301.1493\"},{\"title\":\"nauty and Traces User’s Guide (Version 2.8.9) Brendan D. McKay∗\",\"url\":\"https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/nauty/nug28.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the topics in your query:\n\n## Graph Isomorphism and Nauty\n\nNauty (No AUTomorphisms, Yes?) is a software package that efficiently computes automorphism groups and canonical labelings. In practice, Nauty uses sophisticated pruning and partitioning techniques to avoid generating all permutations, making it feasible for large graphs.\n\n## Canonical Normalization\n\nA key concept used by nauty and other tools is partition refinement (partition = colouring). The process of finding the canonical member of the isomorphism class containing a given object is called canonical labeling. Two labeled objects which are isomorphic become identical when they are canonically labeled.\n\n## Constraint Programming Applications\n\nAn interesting application appears in graph search problems: Complete symmetry breaking for graph search problems can be introduced by modeling, in terms of constraints, the same ideas underlying the algorithm applied in tools like nauty. This suggests that nauty's canonical normalization techniques have been adapted for constraint programming to break symmetries during search.\n\n## Related Tools\n\nBliss is used for graph canonical labeling and excels in canonical labeling and symmetry detection, making it a go-to for graph normalization.\n\nHowever, I did not find specific results about \"nogood learning\" in relation to these topics. The search results focus primarily on the theoretical foundations and practical implementations of canonical labeling and graph isomorphism testing rather than constraint programming nogoods learning mechanisms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"477b146b-dfec-4c0d-951e-fdc314880481","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:37.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"135eff15-3711-45e9-8a24-f72739cffc57","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"30c94437-d0ec-47af-a439-1e03ba4ed736","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"ae3c21075cb388b14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DN27z4LFzU1wBo8RKGsZuq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Benders cut sharing parallel decomposition cross-scenario reuse\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Scalable parallel Benders decomposition for stochastic linear programming - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167819197000446\"},{\"title\":\"A Bender’s Algorithm of Decomposition Used for the Parallel Machine Problem of Robotic Cell\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/9/15/1730\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benders_decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"Parallelization and aggregation ofnested Benders decomposition | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/A:1018996821817\"},{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition Using Graph Modeling and Multi-Parametric Programming - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12616700/\"},{\"title\":\"A Closest Benders Cut Selection Scheme for Accelerating the Benders Decomposition Algorithm | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2022.1207\"},{\"title\":\"A converging Benders’ decomposition algorithm for two-stage\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/8165.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Multicut Benders decomposition algorithm for process supply chain planning under uncertainty | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-011-0974-4\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] The Benders Dual Decomposition Method | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/The-Benders-Dual-Decomposition-Method-Rahmaniani-Ahmed/53a33922bc4af4bac06d00cdff337eab839d3f54\"},{\"title\":\"AMPL Development Tutorial 5/6 – Parallelizing Subproblem Solves in Benders Decomposition — AMPL Colaboratory\",\"url\":\"https://ampl.com/colab/notebooks/ampl-development-tutorial-56-parallelizing-subproblem-solves-in-benders-decomposition.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Benders decomposition with related topics on cut sharing, parallel processing, and scenario-based approaches:\n\n## Overview\n\nBenders decomposition is a technique in mathematical optimization that allows the solution of very large linear programming problems that have a special block structure, which often occurs in applications such as stochastic programming where uncertainty is usually represented with scenarios.\n\n## Benders Cuts\n\nIf the subproblem determines that the fixed first-stage decisions are in fact infeasible, then so-called Benders cuts are generated and added to the master problem, which is then re-solved until no cuts can be generated.\n\n## Parallel Decomposition\n\nA scalable parallel implementation of the classical Benders decomposition algorithm for two-stage stochastic linear programs can be developed using a primal-dual, path-following algorithm for solving the scenario subproblems to develop a parallel implementation that alleviates the difficulties of load balancing.\n\n## Cross-Scenario Reuse and Cut Strategies\n\nFor two-stage stochastic programs, all scenario subproblems are structurally identical; they differ only in the realized values of the uncertain data. This homogeneity is a significant advantage, as it allows for a single surrogate to be generated once in an offline step and then reused for every subproblem solve across all Benders iterations.\n\nThe main idea is to add one cut per realization of uncertainty to the master problem in each iteration, that is, as many Benders cuts as the number of scenarios added to the master problem in each iteration.\n\nThe search results show active research in accelerating Benders decomposition through various cut strategies, parallel computation of subproblems, and exploiting the structural homogeneity of scenario-based problems for computational efficiency.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c77182db-522f-48ea-b89d-81d458668027","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:41:38.996Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30c94437-d0ec-47af-a439-1e03ba4ed736","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
